(:doc :symbol "asl/host/tests/floorRtTest.asl#" :text "FLOORRT gate: the collector's fatal errors leave through the C floor's own exit (gcFloor.h), not value.c's aslError. A program that keeps every cons cell live exhausts an ASL_GC_MAX_MIB heap; built natively and linked against libaslrt.a it exits with asl-host run's code and error line, while the same program with a short list fits the cap on both. The floor objects of libaslrt.a, gcAsl.o (the ASL collector, which replaced gc.o there in GCASL-2) and strFloor.o, carry no undefined reference to value.c's error machinery (aslError, aslErrorRethrow, aslErrorHandlerGet, aslErrorHandlerSet, aslErrorMsg).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/host/tests/floorRtTest.asl#hostErrorLine" :text "The ERR_<CODE>: <message> part of an asl-host run failure, reported as 'FAIL <file>: ERR_...: ... (after N asserts)'.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/host/tests/floorRtTest.asl#build" :text "Writes the program, builds it with asl1 and links it against libaslrt.a; returns the source path.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/host/tests/floorRtTest.asl#undefinedNames" :text "Symbol names of nm -u output, with the Mach-O leading underscore dropped.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/host/tests/floorRtTest.asl#valueErrorNames" :text "value.c's error machinery: the raise, its rethrow, the handler stack and the message buffer.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/host/tests/floorRtTest.asl#testFloorObject" :text "member of libaslrt.a, extracted with ar p, has undefined references (needs is one it must have, so the list is real) and none to value.c's error machinery: aslError, its rethrow, handler stack or message buffer (the collector's raise guards reach them through gcFloorGuard).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/host/tests/nativeOnlySigTest.asl#" :text "Native-only signature gate: the host checker accepts the handoff module and its native fixture, while executing a native-route-only call on the VM fails explicitly with the missing capability and builtin name.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/host/tools/genInventory.asl#" :text "U13 host floor inventory: nm -P over the host objects union a column-0 definition scan of src/*.c, classified against tests/acceptance/r1Host/floor.asn")
(:doc :symbol "asl/host/tools/genInventory.asl#aslObjects" :text "Archive members compiled from ASL, not from asl/host/src: libaslrt.a's gcAsl.o is asl-target-llvm/gcRoute's collector module (GCASL-2) and rtAbi.o asl-target-llvm/rtAbi's runtime ABI module (RT-ABI), so they have no C floor rows.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/host/tools/genInventory.asl#structBody?" :text "struct W brace opens a type")
(:doc :symbol "asl/host/tools/genInventory.asl#bodyFollows?" :text "a close paren before any semicolon, then brace")
(:doc :symbol "asl/host/tools/genInventory.asl#fnFrom" :text "leftmost name whose parameter list opens a body")
(:doc :symbol "asl/host/tools/genInventory.asl#declaredAt" :text "name, optional bounds, then assignment, semicolon or comma")
(:doc :symbol "asl/host/tools/genInventory.asl#typedFrom" :text "type word, stars, optional const, name")
(:doc :symbol "asl/host/tools/genInventory.asl#varName" :text "optional prefixes are tried taken first")
(:doc :symbol "asl/host/tools/genInventory.asl#cleanFrom" :text "mode 0 code, 1 comment, 2-3 literal")
(:doc :symbol "asl/host/tools/genInventory.asl#declText" :text "declaration to its top-level semicolon, literals removed")
(:doc :symbol "asl/host/tools/genInventory.asl#lastName" :text "last top-level word before the initializer")
(:doc :symbol "asl/host/tools/genInventory.asl#sameLineRest" :text "text after a declaration ending on this line")
(:doc :symbol "asl/host/tools/genInventory.asl#floorBlocks" :text "block of each (:block :symbols list in floor.asn")
(:doc :symbol "asl/host/tools/genInventory.asl#floorRuling" :text "FLOORRT ruling (lead, 2026-10-04): native GC roots and runtime init in abi.c, and strFloor.c (the string allocators behind the three string primitives and the floor error exit), are memory floor that floor.asn does not name yet")
(:doc :symbol "asl/host/tools/genInventory.asl#budgets" :text "valueGc raised to 1000 for conservative object lookup")
(:doc :symbol "asl/host/tests/runtimeNoHostTest.asl#members" :text "RUNTIME-NOHOST: build.sh into an empty out dir and host cache, given an earlier libaslrt.a (ASL_NATIVE_RT), emits gcAsl, rtAbi and rtFloor with native emitters a seed asl1 compiled; a sampler records the build's process tree every 0.2 s (descendants of the build pid), which must show the seed asl1 and never asl-host, and the archive's members must equal the host-emitted ones in asl/host/out/libaslrt.a byte for byte")
(:doc :symbol "asl/host/tests/runtimeNoHostTest.asl#sampler" :text "the build with a sampler beside it: each round appends the argv of every descendant of the build pid to SNAP")
(:doc :symbol "asl/host/tests/archiveKeyTest.asl#members" :text "ARCHIVE-KEY: two runtime rebuilds into separate out dirs and host caches, two seconds apart, emit equal members and so must pack byte-equal libaslrt.a archives (ar without member dates), because bin/asl's native key and nativeTest's toolchain key hash the archive's bytes; an archive stamped with its build time changes those keys on every rebuild")
(:doc :symbol "asl/host/tests/archiveKeyTest.asl#rebuildTwice" :text "two builds from the same earlier runtime (ASL_NATIVE_RT), a pause between them so member dates would differ")
(:doc :symbol "asl/host/tests/runtimeSeedTest.asl#members" :text "RUNTIME-SEED: a fresh copy of the tree (asl, bin, tools and the root manifests, no asl/host/out, an empty host cache, no ASL_NATIVE_RT) runs build.sh and then bin/asl test of a probe suite; build.sh compiles a bootstrap libaslrt.a from the runtime IR beside the asl1 seed, so a sampler of the whole tree (every 0.2 s, descendants of the script pid) never sees asl-host, sees the seed asl1, the probe is served by a native binary, and the members equal asl/host/out/libaslrt.a's byte for byte")
(:doc :symbol "asl/host/tests/runtimeSeedTest.asl#sampler" :text "the script with a sampler beside it: each round appends the argv of every descendant of the script pid to SNAP")
(:doc :symbol "asl/host/tests/runtimeSeedTest.asl#freshClone" :text "build the runtime from nothing, then serve the probe natively; SERVED_STOP_PID lets the probe walk up to this script")
